 "rules": "Per type, per arm (own = own heads 170631/170706, decline = direct read 169526): an item on a capture whose K5 disagreement exceeds tau (TAU.json) takes the arm's banked answer; every other item keeps the baseline's (171253). Item score: score_nfa.item_score (0 for a capped read, else output.scores.answer) for 171253 and own rows; the direct read's compact score, zeroed on a forced close, token cap, error finish or parse failure (capped_zeroed). Difference swap - baseline in points over all 150 items (unflagged items differ by 0); paired room bootstrap (resample room_key with replacement, ratio of sums, 10,000 draws, seed 20261115, h1eval.statistics draw order); Bonferroni 99.375% two-sided interval (2 arms x 4 types); 95% two-sided interval. Decidable type: >= 10 flagged items in >= 3 rooms and ceiling 100 x flagged / 150 >= 2 points. Lane ruling (F1, before any score): a decidable type with fewer than 6 flagged rooms is labelled \"can close, cannot pass\" (a bootstrap draw with no flagged room gives exactly 0, so its 0.3125th percentile cannot exceed 0); it may close but never pass. A pass needs >= 6 flagged rooms plus the decidable rule. Worth building: some type that can pass and arm with difference >= +1.0 and 99.375% lower bound > 0. Closed: on every decidable type both arms' 95% upper bounds < +1.0. Too few: no decidable type. Else undecided. Conservative choices (not fixed by the design): distance passes only if it passes against both 171253 distance reads (read 1, the pinned candidates_argmax baseline; read 0 null_argmax, which holds the registered 26.93 and matches the own arm's selector) and closes only if it closes against both; a decline-arm pass counts as undecided while the direct read's anchor frames are unchecked. Oracle: best of the three arms per flagged item (ceiling, reported only). Fragile-flag sensitivity: flags of captures with tau/2 <= disagreement <= 2 tau flipped, everything repriced and the reading reported beside.",
